's Training Log","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/markkos-training-log/208986","site":"T Nation · 10000 posts · 2015"},{"title":"The Flame-Free Confession Thread II","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/the-flame-free-confession-thread-ii/248113","site":"T Nation · 9998 posts · 2018"},{"title":"More Trouble Than I Am Worth: Chaos Is The Plan (T3hPwnisher Log)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/more-trouble-than-i-am-worth-chaos-is-the-plan-t3hpwnisher-log/276232","site":"T Nation · 8675 posts · 2021"},{"title":"Per aspera ad astra (strongman Koestrizer)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/per-aspera-ad-astra-strongman-koestrizer/213205","site":"T Nation · 8404 posts · 2015"},{"title":"Things That Piss You Off","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/things-that-piss-you-off/163775","site":"T Nation · 7426 posts · 2011"},{"title":"Things That Make You Chuckle","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/things-that-make-you-chuckle/240079","site":"T Nation · 6256 posts · 2018"},{"title":"The Tactical Life","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/the-tactical-life/232312","site":"T Nation · 5251 posts · 2017"},{"title":"Dodgin’ Dadbods: Fortitude Training","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/dodgin-dadbods-fortitude-training/240588","site":"T Nation · 4913 posts · 2018"},{"title":"Russian Military Buildup Outside Ukraine","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/russian-military-buildup-outside-ukraine/276763","site":"T Nation · 3353 posts · 2022"},{"title":"US Presidential Election Predictions","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/us-presidential-election-predictions/270025","site":"T Nation · 3253 posts · 2020"},{"title":"Dchris's Grappling with Age","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/dchriss-grappling-with-age/224841","site":"T Nation · 2559 posts · 2016"},{"title":":fire: Post Your Hot Takes... Even the Oddly Specific Ones","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/post-your-hot-takes-even-the-oddly-specific-ones/283831","site":"T Nation · 1913 posts · 2023"},{"title":"The War on Drugs","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/the-war-on-drugs/265165","site":"T Nation · 1909 posts · 2020"},{"title":"Vinny's Strongman Log II","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/vinnys-strongman-log-ii/215150","site":"T Nation · 1871 posts · 2016"},{"title":"White Supremacy: \"A Hoax\"?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/white-supremacy-a-hoax/259639","site":"T Nation · 1636 posts · 2019"}],"news":[],"social":[],"web":[{"title":"Bow tie — Grokipedia","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Bow_tie"},{"title":"Bow tie - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bow_tie"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Jawline & face shape","chain":["Small bow sits just below the jaw","Draws the eye to the face and neck","Sharper, more put-together overall look"],"effect":"direct","text":"A bow tie places a compact accent right under the face, so people use it to look polished and to add a memorable focal point at the collar. Choice of shape and size changes how it frames the jaw."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Bow_tie","lead":["A bow tie is a neckwear piece made from a strip of fabric tied in a symmetrical bow at the collar. Types include pre-tied (a bow sewn onto a neck band), clip-on, and the traditional self-tie, also called freestyle.[1]","For appearance, it works as a style accessory that frames the jaw and lower face and signals formality. It is the classic neckwear of black-tie and white-tie evening dress, and is also worn by classical musicians, at weddings, and by some people as a signature look.[1]","Its history is tied to the cravat: scarves worn by Croatian mercenaries during the Thirty Years' War were adopted by the French upper classes, and historians are unsure whether the cravat evolved into the bow tie and the four-in-hand necktie or the bow tie came first.[1]"],"infobox":[["Type","Neckwear"],["Styles","Self-tie, pre-tied, clip-on[1]"],["Shapes","Bat wing, butterfly (thistle), diamond point[1]"],["Classic setting","Black-tie and white-tie evening wear[1]"],["Origins","17th-century neck scarves; cravat tradition[1]"]],"sections":[{"h":"Design and types","paras":["Pre-tied bow ties are sewn to a band that clips closed, clip-on versions attach directly to collar points, and the self-tie is the traditional strip tied by hand.[1] Common shapes are the bat wing with parallel sides, the thistle or butterfly, and the diamond point, which is pointed at both ends.[1] Fixed-length ties suit formal wing-collar shirts, while adjustable ties suit softer collars.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Occasions and etiquette","paras":["Black-tie and white-tie evening wear is the classic setting, and bow ties are also common at weddings and among classical musicians. Ready-tied versions are generally considered a faux pas at black- or white-tie events but are common at occasions such as school proms.[1] Pediatricians often wear them because infants cannot grab them the way they can a necktie.[1] In the 1980s some professional women wore them with tailored suits.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Cultural associations","paras":["Commentators have noted both a possible comeback among men and a reputation for conservatism and nerdiness.[1] Public figures known for wearing them include the biochemist Fritz Lipmann, Belgian prime minister Elio Di Rupo, Bill Nye and Paul Reubens as Pee-wee Herman.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[{"year":"17th century","event":"Croatian mercenaries in the Thirty Years' War wear neck scarves later adopted in France as cravats.[1]"},{"year":"18th-19th century","event":"French upper classes adopt the cravat; related styles such as the lavalliere appear.[1]"}],"refs":[{"title":"Bow tie (Wikipedia)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bow_tie","source":"Wikipedia","year":null,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Bow tie (Grokipedia)","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Bow_tie","source":"Grokipedia","year":null,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"MarkKO's Training Log","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/markkos-training-log/208986","site":"T Nation · 10000 posts · 2015"},{"title":"The Flame-Free Confession Thread II","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/the-flame-free-confession-thread-ii/248113","site":"T Nation · 9998 posts · 2018"},{"title":"More Trouble Than I Am Worth: Chaos Is The Plan (T3hPwnisher Log)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/more-trouble-than-i-am-worth-chaos-is-the-plan-t3hpwnisher-log/276232","site":"T Nation · 8675 posts · 2021"},{"title":"Per aspera ad astra (strongman Koestrizer)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/per-aspera-ad-astra-strongman-koestrizer/213205","site":"T Nation · 8404 posts · 2015"},{"title":"Things That Piss You Off","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/things-that-piss-you-off/163775","site":"T Nation · 7426 posts · 2011"},{"title":"Things That Make You Chuckle","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/things-that-make-you-chuckle/240079","site":"T Nation · 6256 posts · 2018"}]}